{
  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-3221",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-3221: Important priority package update for bind",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-13 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-13 19:44:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Amazon Linux–vended DNS resolvers shipped with an older DNSSEC root signing key. For hosts configured with DNSSEC validation enabled, this could result in DNS resolution failures, including for names in unsigned zones. This applies where the resolver is still using the trust anchor shipped in the package; resolvers that already picked up the new root key via RFC 5011 are unaffected.\n\nOn 11 October 2026 at 14:00 UTC the DNS root zone began signing with KSK-2024 (key tag 38696), replacing KSK-2017 (key tag 20326). The packaged trust anchor files contained only KSK-2017, so an affected resolver cannot validate the root DNSKEY RRset and returns SERVFAIL.\n\nThe updated packages include an updated root signing key.",
